  "limitations": [
    "Synchronous in-memory fake; no physical backend throughput claim.",
    "Identical consumer fixture and request across lanes, including assertions.",
    "Current canonical APIs have no equivalent 0.2 authority contract; control is the earlier coherent 0.3 implementation.",
    "Seven alternated cycles: 100 individual samples for one-event history and 31 for 32/256-event histories; 1000 timer controls; three warmups.",
    "Complete signed histories of 1,32,256 commits; verification and already-verified checkpoint/rebuild paths measured separately. Memory sink/fresh handles and injected checkpoint ACK loss do not prove physical durability.",
    "Process totals include identical fixed generation/verification of all three fixture sizes.",
    "Equal-length lane executable names and 128-byte arguments; trim truncates without reallocation.",
    "Matched controls use the same action-count environment. Process exit skips destruction, so frees are not leak qualification.",
    "1000,100,10 actions for 1,32,256 events respectively; control-subtracted counts describe this fixture, not arbitrary backend memory.",
    "Allocation-only processes use independently recorded CPU cores; no allocation execution times are latency observations. Full control and candidate sources, actual timeout and intentional handoff remain separately retained."
  ]
